"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nPerson Note\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nOn Find a Grave page:<br />\nLydia Yeaple Hittle was born in Pennsylvania and nothing else has yet been learned of her early years. She became the second spouse of Michael Hittle (1776-1855) of Fishing Creek, Bloom TWP, Northumberland County (later changed to Columbia County) Pennsylvania. Michael's first wife (name unknown) died circa 1806 leaving him with four small children. Between 1812-1816, Lydia became Michael's second wife. In 1819/1820 Michael and Lydia relocated to Greene County Ohio where Michael's older brother by two years, George Hittle, had moved before the War of 1812. Here, Michael and Lydia had a seventh child, Jacob Hittle (1820-1905) before moving further west and settling in Rush County Indiana by 1824. Here they remained for the next 25 years, raising their large family. Michael was a Blacksmith and farmer.\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nIn 1846 Michael and Lydia followed some of their grown sons to Monroe County Iowa and they were among the original pioneers to settle at a place known as Bremen, 1 mile east of Lovilia. Michael passed away in 1855. Lydia went to her eternal rest in 1860.\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\nThe offspring of Michael and Lydia Yeaple Hittle were:\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n--Michael Hittle B. 11 July 1816 Fishing Creek, Bloom TWP, Columbia County, PA\n</p>\n<p>\nD. 15 May 1878 at Lovilia, Union TWP, Monroe County IA\n</p>\n<p>\n--Henry Hittle B. 15 Jan 1818 near Dayton, Greene County, OH\n</p>\n<p>\nD, 14 Aug 1897 at Lovilia, Union TWP, Monroe County IA\n</p>\n<p>\n--Jacob Hittle* B. 06 Jun 1820 near Dayton, Greene County, OH\n</p>\n<p>\nD, 15 Feb 1905 at Good Hope, near Castana, Kennebec TWP\n</p>\n<p>\nMonona County, IA\n</p>\n<p>\n--Mary Ann Hittle B. 1823, Probably Rushville, Rush County, IN\n</p>\n<p>\nD. Post-1895 (Married to Samuel Kinton)\n</p>\n<p>\n--Isaac Hittle B. 07 Dec 1824, Rushville, Rush County, IN\n</p>\n<p>\nD. 1904, Hillsdale, Miami County, KS\n</p>\n<p>\n--Hartsell Phillip Hittle * (AKA: \"Harts\" B. 1827/28, Rushville, Rush County, IN\n</p>\n<p>\nD, 14 June, 1894 at Lovilia, Monroe County, IA\n</p>\n<p>\n--John H. Hittle* B.30 Jun 1830, Rushville, Rush County, IN\n</p>\n<p>\nD. 01 Jul 1895, Lovilia, Union County, Monroe County, IA\n</p>\n<p>\n--Ambulance Hittle (\"Abalena\") B. ca. 1831/33 Rushville, Rush County IN\n</p>\n<p>\nD. post-1895. probably at Maple Landing,\n</p>\n<p>\nMonona County, IA (Married to George\n</p>\n<p>\nSappinfield)\n</p>\n<p>\n* CIVIL WAR VETERANS:\n</p>\n<p>\n* Jacob Hittle, Corporal, CO A, 36th Iowa Infantry Regiment 1862-1865\n</p>\n<p>\n* John H. Hittle, Company D, 22nd Iowa Infantry Regiment 1862-1865\n</p>\n<p>\n* Isaac Hittle, Southern Border Brigade, Iowa Home Guard Militia\n</p>\n<p>\n* Hartsell P. Hittle, Southern Border Brigade, Iowa Home Guard Militia\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
